      ],
      "acceptable_supporting": [
        "assertion"
      ]
    },
    "description": "The Grocer pricing service calculates basket totals in InvoicePricing, DiscountSchedule, and TaxRule. Today each component reads mutable configuration, a cached exchange rate, or counters hidden in the invoice while producing a result, so two identical baskets can receive different totals when requests are close together. The pricing rules must instead be predictable: given immutable basket lines, a snapshot of discount rules, the applicable tax jurisdictions, and currency conversion factors, the same inputs must always produce the same line totals, tax, and final amount. Each calculation must leave its inputs and any running total unchanged, while the application service remains responsible for loading snapshots and recording the resulting invoice. Tests must be able to exercise tax and rebate combinations without constructing repositories, clocks, or cached market data. The team also wants money arithmetic to remain valid at every combination boundary, including rejection of additions across different currencies. This decision concerns where pricing behavior lives and how it is evaluated, not how the invoice is persisted or how the web request is handled.",
    "decision_statement": "Move tax, rebate, and total calculations behind operations that derive results solely from explicit immutable inputs and never modify those inputs or shared state.",
    "notes": "side-effect-free-function primary: the same immutable inputs must always yield the same totals with no mutation of inputs or shared state; closure-of-operations and standalone-class are the composition and testability near-misses; assertion supports cross-currency rejection."
  },
